"type":"text","text":"The edge’s position: a new one, or on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyList"},{"type":"text","text":", which is simple, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"existing edge’s."}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the source is already placed before the target, the cost is two array reads plus the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"base’s insertion. Otherwise Pearce and Kelly’s reordering runs, O(‖δ‖ + δ log δ) for the δ"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices it visits between the endpoints’ places; see the type’s documentation. A rejection"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"allocates nothing once the reordering’s scratch has grown."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AcyclicEdgeError.selfLoop"},{"type":"text","text":" for a self-loop, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".cycle"},{"type":"text","text":" when the edge would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"close a cycle; then nothing changes, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bidirectionalShortestPath(from: edge.target, to: edge.source)"},{"type":"text","text":" (Traversal) is a path the edge would close. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"try?"},{"type":"text","text":" turns a rejection"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"into "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Throws","style":"note"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule\/documentation\/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule\/DirectedAcyclicGraph\/insert(edge:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/directedacyclicgraphmodule\/directedacyclicgraph\/insert(edge:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hier